lessons.push({
  title: "Flask Fundamentals: Routes, Requests and JSON Responses",
  minutes: 55,
  learn: ["Create a Flask application and define routes", "Read path, query and JSON data from the request", "Return JSON with status codes and handle errors", "Test an app with Flask's test client"],
  why: "Flask is a small, readable framework that teaches how web back-ends work. Many companies use it for APIs and internal tools, and the ideas transfer to every other framework.",
  realWorld: "A small internal dashboard, a webhook receiver, a machine-learning model served as an API.",
  simple: "A Flask <strong>route</strong> maps a URL and method to a Python function. The function returns data (a dict becomes JSON) and optionally a status code.",
  detail: `<p><strong>Requires:</strong> <code>python -m pip install flask</code> (Flask 3). Run a development server with <code>flask --app app run --debug</code>; never use the debug server in production (use gunicorn, waitress or a container).</p>
<pre style="background:#16181c;color:#d8dee9;padding:12px 14px;border-radius:8px"><code>from flask import Flask, jsonify, request, abort\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.get("/students/&lt;int:student_id&gt;")\ndef get_student(student_id):\n    ...\n\n@app.post("/students")\ndef create_student():\n    data = request.get_json()\n    ...\n    return jsonify(student), 201</code></pre>
${table(["Piece", "Purpose"], [["<code>@app.get/post/put/delete(path)</code>", "route for one method (or <code>@app.route(path, methods=[...])</code>)"], ["<code>&lt;int:id&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;string:name&gt;</code>", "typed path variables"], ["<code>request.args</code>", "query parameters (<code>request.args.get(\"page\", 1, type=int)</code>)"], ["<code>request.get_json()</code>", "parsed JSON body (400/415 if invalid)"], ["<code>jsonify(...)</code> or a returned dict", "JSON response"], ["<code>abort(404)</code>, <code>@app.errorhandler</code>", "raise HTTP errors; shape error responses"], ["<code>@app.before_request</code>", "run code before every request (auth, logging)"], ["<code>Blueprint</code>", "group routes into modules"], ["application factory <code>create_app()</code>", "build the app for different configs and tests"], ["<code>app.test_client()</code>", "call routes without a server"]])}
<h3>Practices</h3>
<ul><li>Keep configuration in environment variables; the secret key must come from outside the code.</li><li>Validate input (Flask does not do it for you): use a library such as Pydantic or marshmallow for larger apps.</li><li>Return correct status codes and consistent error JSON.</li><li>One function per route; business logic in separate modules so it can be tested without HTTP.</li></ul>`,
  syntax: { code: `from flask import Flask, jsonify, request\napp = Flask(__name__)\n@app.get("/ping")\ndef ping():\n    return {"pong": True}\nclient = app.test_client()`, note: "A dict return value becomes a JSON response." },
  diagram: chain("A Flask request", "Left to right: the URL is matched to a route, the view function reads the request, returns data and a status code, and Flask sends the HTTP response.",
    [{ k: "io", t: "GET /students/7" }, { k: "proc", t: "route matches\n<int:id>" }, { k: "proc", t: "view function\nruns" }, { k: "io", t: "JSON + status" }], { w: 140, gap: 30, hgt: 58 }),
  example: { code: `from flask import Flask, jsonify, request, abort\n\nSTUDENTS = {1: {"id": 1, "name": "Asha", "dept": "CSE"}, 2: {"id": 2, "name": "Ravi", "dept": "ECE"}}\n\ndef create_app():\n    app = Flask(__name__)\n\n    @app.get("/students")\n    def list_students():\n        dept = request.args.get("dept")\n        rows = [s for s in STUDENTS.values() if dept is None or s["dept"] == dept]\n        return jsonify(sorted(rows, key=lambda s: s["id"]))\n\n    @app.get("/students/<int:student_id>")\n    def get_student(student_id):\n        student = STUDENTS.get(student_id)\n        if student is None:\n            abort(404)\n        return jsonify(student)\n\n    @app.post("/students")\n    def create_student():\n        data = request.get_json(silent=True) or {}\n        if not data.get("name"):\n            return jsonify({"error": "name is required"}), 422\n        new_id = max(STUDENTS) + 1\n        STUDENTS[new_id] = {"id": new_id, "name": data["name"], "dept": data.get("dept", "NA")}\n        return jsonify(STUDENTS[new_id]), 201, {"Location": f"/students/{new_id}"}\n\n    @app.errorhandler(404)\n    def not_found(error):\n        return jsonify({"error": "not found"}), 404\n\n    return app\n\nclient = create_app().test_client()\nprint(client.get("/students").get_json())\nprint(client.get("/students?dept=ECE").get_json())\nprint(client.get("/students/1").get_json(), client.get("/students/99").status_code, client.get("/students/99").get_json())\nr = client.post("/students", json={"name": "Zoya", "dept": "CSE"})\nprint(r.status_code, r.headers["Location"], r.get_json())\nprint(client.post("/students", json={}).status_code, client.delete("/students/1").status_code)\nprint(client.get("/students/abc").status_code)`, out: `[{'dept': 'CSE', 'id': 1, 'name': 'Asha'}, {'dept': 'ECE', 'id': 2, 'name': 'Ravi'}]\n[{'dept': 'ECE', 'id': 2, 'name': 'Ravi'}]\n{'dept': 'CSE', 'id': 1, 'name': 'Asha'} 404 {'error': 'not found'}\n201 /students/3 {'dept': 'CSE', 'id': 3, 'name': 'Zoya'}\n422 405\n404` },
  lineByLine: [["create_app()", "The application factory: builds a fresh app (handy for tests)."], ["@app.get(\"/students/<int:student_id>\")", "The converter turns the path part into an int; non-numbers do not match (404)."], ["request.args.get(\"dept\")", "Optional query filter."], ["abort(404) + errorhandler", "Raises an HTTP error that the handler turns into JSON."], ["return jsonify(...), 201, {...}", "A body, a status code and extra headers."], ["client.delete(...) = 405", "There is no DELETE route, so Flask answers Method Not Allowed."]],
  dryRun: { intro: "<code>GET /students/99</code>:", headers: ["Step", "What happens"], rows: [["route match", "student_id = 99"], ["lookup", "STUDENTS.get(99) is None"], ["abort(404)", "the error handler returns JSON {'error': 'not found'}"]] },
  realExample: { intro: "A health-check endpoint and a before-request hook that adds a header to every response.", code: `from flask import Flask\napp = Flask(__name__)\n@app.get("/health")\ndef health():\n    return {"status": "ok"}\n@app.after_request\ndef add_header(response):\n    response.headers["X-Service"] = "students-api"\n    return response\nr = app.test_client().get("/health")\nprint(r.status_code, r.get_json(), r.headers["X-Service"])`, out: `200 {'status': 'ok'} students-api` },
  mistakes: ["Running the debug server in production.", "Trusting input without validation.", "Storing state in module globals when the app runs with several workers.", "Hard-coding the secret key.", "Putting all logic inside view functions."],
  practices: ["Use the application factory and blueprints.", "Test routes with the test client.", "Return JSON errors consistently."],
  interview: ["What is a Flask route?", "What is the application factory?", "How do you read JSON from a request?", "How do you test a Flask app?"],
  practiceQs: ["How do you accept an integer id in the URL?", "Which decorator handles a 404 for the whole app?", "How do you return 201 with a header?", "Why not run flask --debug in production?"],
  revision: ["@app.get/post(path); <int:id>.", "request.args, request.get_json().", "jsonify, status codes, abort, errorhandler.", "test_client(); factory; blueprints."],
  hinglish: "Flask mein route URL aur method ko ek Python function se jodta hai. dict return karo to JSON ban jata hai, status code saath mein de sakte ho. request.get_json() se body milti hai aur test_client() se bina server ke test hota hai.",
  quiz: [
    mcq("What does @app.get(\"/ping\") do?", ["Registers a GET route", "Starts the server", "Creates a database", "Imports a module"], 0, "It maps the URL and method to the function."),
    mcq("How do you read the query parameter ?page=2?", ["request.args.get(\"page\")", "request.json", "request.form", "page()"], 0, "request.args holds the query."),
    mcq("What does a Flask view returning ({'a': 1}, 201) send?", ["A JSON body with status 201", "Text with status 200", "A redirect", "Nothing"], 0, "Body plus status code."),
    mcq("Which tool calls routes without a running server?", ["app.test_client()", "curl only", "print", "gunicorn"], 0, "The test client."),
    mcq("What is the application factory used for?", ["Creating configurable app instances (tests, environments)", "Creating databases", "Sorting routes", "Installing Flask"], 0, "create_app().")
  ],
  tasks: [task("Route matcher", "Read n route patterns of the form METHOD /path/<int:name> HANDLER, then requests of the form METHOD /path. A pattern segment <int:name> matches digits and captures the value. For each request print HANDLER followed by the captured values as name=value (in order), or 404 when no route matches, or 405 when the path matches a route but not for that method (404 takes lower priority than 405).", "n = int(input())\n# read the routes, then the requests\n", `import sys\nn = int(input())\nroutes = []\nfor _ in range(n):\n    method, pattern, handler = input().split()\n    routes.append((method, pattern.strip("/").split("/"), handler))\ndef match(pattern, parts):\n    if len(pattern) != len(parts):\n        return None\n    captured = []\n    for p, part in zip(pattern, parts):\n        if p.startswith("<int:") and p.endswith(">"):\n            if not part.isdigit():\n                return None\n            captured.append(f"{p[5:-1]}={part}")\n        elif p != part:\n            return None\n    return captured\nfor line in sys.stdin:\n    if not line.strip():\n        continue\n    method, path = line.split()\n    parts = path.strip("/").split("/")\n    answer = "404"\n    for m, pattern, handler in routes:\n        captured = match(pattern, parts)\n        if captured is None:\n            continue\n        if m == method:\n            answer = " ".join([handler] + captured)\n            break\n        answer = "405"\n    print(answer)`, [["3\nGET /students list_students\nGET /students/<int:id> get_student\nPOST /students create_student\nGET /students/7\nPOST /students/7\nGET /courses", "get_student id=7\n405\n404"], ["1\nGET /ping ping\nGET /ping", "ping"]], [["3\nGET /students list_students\nGET /students/<int:id> get_student\nPOST /students create_student\nGET /students/7\nPOST /students/7\nGET /courses", "get_student id=7\n405\n404"], ["1\nGET /ping ping\nGET /ping", "ping"], ["2\nGET /a/<int:x>/b/<int:y> pair\nDELETE /a/1/b/2 gone\nGET /a/10/b/20\nDELETE /a/1/b/2\nPUT /a/1/b/2", "pair x=10 y=20\ngone\n405"], ["1\nGET /students/<int:id> s\nGET /students/abc", "404"]])],
});

