lessons.push({
  title: "FastAPI Fundamentals: Type Hints, Validation and Automatic Docs",
  minutes: 60,
  learn: ["Define path, query and body parameters with type hints", "Validate requests with Pydantic models", "Return typed responses and handle errors", "Use the automatic OpenAPI/Swagger documentation"],
  why: "FastAPI turns Python type hints into validation, serialisation and interactive documentation, and it supports async code. It is one of the most popular modern API frameworks and a frequent choice in new projects.",
  realWorld: "Production APIs for mobile apps and machine-learning models; the documentation page it generates is used by front-end teams to try the API.",
  simple: "You write ordinary functions with type hints. FastAPI reads the hints to parse and check input (returning <strong>422</strong> with details on bad data), converts output to JSON, and publishes an <strong>OpenAPI</strong> description with a Swagger UI at <code>/docs</code>.",
  detail: `<p><strong>Requires:</strong> <code>python -m pip install fastapi httpx uvicorn</code> (httpx powers the TestClient). Run with <code>uvicorn main:app --reload</code>; browse <code>/docs</code> (Swagger UI) and <code>/redoc</code>.</p>
${table(["Feature", "How"], [["path parameter", "<code>@app.get(\"/students/{student_id}\")</code> with <code>student_id: int</code>"], ["query parameter", "any other typed function parameter, with defaults: <code>dept: str | None = None, limit: int = 10</code>"], ["JSON body", "a parameter whose type is a Pydantic model"], ["validation", "automatic; constraints with <code>Field(ge=0, le=120)</code>, <code>min_length</code>, regex"], ["response shape", "<code>response_model=StudentOut</code> filters fields (hide passwords) and documents the schema"], ["status codes", "<code>status_code=201</code>, <code>raise HTTPException(404, \"...\")</code>"], ["dependencies", "<code>Depends(get_db)</code>: reusable pieces such as database sessions and authentication"], ["async", "<code>async def</code> endpoints for I/O-bound work (Module 13)"], ["testing", "<code>fastapi.testclient.TestClient</code>"]])}
<h3>Pydantic models</h3>
<p>A model is a class with typed fields. Pydantic converts compatible values (<code>"5"</code> to <code>5</code> in lax mode), rejects invalid ones and reports every problem with its location. Use separate models for input (<code>StudentIn</code>), output (<code>StudentOut</code>) and the database.</p>
<h3>Why 422?</h3>
<p>The request was well-formed but its content failed validation. The error body lists each failing field (<code>loc</code>, <code>msg</code>, <code>type</code>), so clients know what to fix.</p>`,
  syntax: { code: `from fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\napp = FastAPI()\nclass StudentIn(BaseModel):\n    name: str = Field(min_length=1)\n    age: int = Field(ge=0, le=120)\n@app.post("/students", status_code=201)\ndef create(student: StudentIn): ...`, note: "Type hints are the contract." },
  diagram: chain("Hints become behaviour", "Left to right: a type-hinted function, FastAPI validates the request, runs the function, serialises the result and publishes OpenAPI docs.",
    [{ k: "proc", t: "function with\ntype hints" }, { k: "proc", t: "validate input\n(Pydantic)" }, { k: "proc", t: "run function,\nserialise JSON" }, { k: "term", t: "OpenAPI docs\n/docs" }], { w: 140, gap: 28, hgt: 60 }),
  example: { code: `from fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\napp = FastAPI(title="Students API", version="1.0")\ndb = {}\n\nclass StudentIn(BaseModel):\n    name: str = Field(min_length=1)\n    age: int = Field(ge=0, le=120)\n\nclass StudentOut(StudentIn):\n    id: int\n\n@app.post("/students", response_model=StudentOut, status_code=201)\ndef create(student: StudentIn):\n    new_id = len(db) + 1\n    db[new_id] = StudentOut(id=new_id, **student.model_dump())\n    return db[new_id]\n\n@app.get("/students/{student_id}", response_model=StudentOut)\ndef read(student_id: int):\n    if student_id not in db:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail="student not found")\n    return db[student_id]\n\n@app.get("/students")\ndef list_students(min_age: int = 0, limit: int = 10):\n    return [s for s in db.values() if s.age >= min_age][:limit]\n\nclient = TestClient(app)\nr = client.post("/students", json={"name": "Asha", "age": 20})\nprint(r.status_code, r.json())\nclient.post("/students", json={"name": "Ravi", "age": 17})\nprint(client.get("/students/1").json(), client.get("/students/9").status_code, client.get("/students/9").json())\nprint(client.get("/students", params={"min_age": 18}).json())\nbad = client.post("/students", json={"name": "", "age": 200})\nprint(bad.status_code, sorted(e["loc"][-1] for e in bad.json()["detail"]))\nprint(client.get("/students/abc").status_code, client.get("/students", params={"limit": "x"}).status_code)\nschema = client.get("/openapi.json").json()\nprint(schema["info"]["title"], sorted(schema["paths"]))\nprint(sorted(schema["paths"]["/students"]), client.get("/docs").status_code)`, out: `201 {'name': 'Asha', 'age': 20, 'id': 1}\n{'name': 'Asha', 'age': 20, 'id': 1} 404 {'detail': 'student not found'}\n[{'name': 'Asha', 'age': 20, 'id': 1}]\n422 ['age', 'name']\n422 422\nStudents API ['/students', '/students/{student_id}']\n['get', 'post'] 200` },
  lineByLine: [["Field(min_length=1)", "A constraint FastAPI enforces and documents."], ["response_model=StudentOut", "Output is validated and shaped; the id field is included."], ["student: StudentIn", "A Pydantic parameter means \"read this from the JSON body\"."], ["min_age: int = 0", "A query parameter with a default and a type; \"x\" for an int gives 422."], ["HTTPException(404)", "A proper error response with a detail message."], ["/openapi.json", "The machine-readable API description; /docs renders it as Swagger UI."]],
  dryRun: { intro: "<code>POST /students {\"name\": \"\", \"age\": 200}</code>:", headers: ["Check", "Result"], rows: [["name min_length=1", "fails (empty)"], ["age le=120", "fails (200)"], ["response", "422 listing both fields; your function never runs"]] },
  realExample: { intro: "A reusable dependency: an API key check shared by several endpoints.", code: `from fastapi import Depends, FastAPI, Header, HTTPException\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\napp = FastAPI()\ndef require_key(x_api_key: str = Header(default="")):\n    if x_api_key != "secret":\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail="invalid key")\n    return x_api_key\n@app.get("/private", dependencies=[Depends(require_key)])\ndef private():\n    return {"data": 42}\nclient = TestClient(app)\nprint(client.get("/private").status_code, client.get("/private", headers={"X-API-Key": "secret"}).json())`, out: `401 {'data': 42}` },
  mistakes: ["Returning ORM objects directly without a response model.", "Using the same model for input and output (leaking fields such as passwords).", "Blocking calls inside <code>async def</code> endpoints.", "Forgetting that constraints belong in the model, not scattered in code.", "Exposing <code>/docs</code> publicly without thought."],
  practices: ["Separate input, output and storage models.", "Use dependencies for auth and database sessions.", "Write tests with TestClient."],
  interview: ["Why is FastAPI fast to develop with?", "What is Pydantic?", "What does response_model do?", "Flask vs FastAPI?"],
  practiceQs: ["Which status does invalid body data return?", "How do you make a query parameter optional?", "What is Depends?", "Where is the OpenAPI schema served?"],
  revision: ["Type hints define path, query and body input.", "Pydantic validates; 422 on failure.", "response_model, status_code, HTTPException.", "/docs and /openapi.json for free."],
  hinglish: "FastAPI type hints se input check karta hai (galat data par 422), JSON jawab banata hai aur /docs par khud documentation deta hai. Body ke liye Pydantic model, query ke liye normal parameters, aur auth ke liye Depends use hota hai.",
  quiz: [
    mcq("What status does FastAPI return when validation fails?", ["400", "404", "422", "500"], 2, "Unprocessable content with details."),
    mcq("Where is the interactive documentation?", ["/docs", "/help", "/swagger.txt", "/api"], 0, "Swagger UI at /docs."),
    mcq("What does Field(ge=0, le=120) do?", ["Sets min and max allowed values", "Creates a database column", "Sorts values", "Hides the field"], 0, "Validation constraints."),
    mcq("What is response_model for?", ["Shapes and validates the output", "Chooses the HTTP method", "Starts the server", "Imports a model"], 0, "It filters and documents the response."),
    mcq("What is Depends used for?", ["Reusable pieces like authentication and database sessions", "Sorting lists", "Defining models", "Running tests"], 0, "Dependency injection.")
  ],
  tasks: [task("Validate a JSON body", "Read one line holding a JSON object. Validate it with these rules: name must be a non-empty string; age must be an integer from 0 to 120 (a boolean is not an integer); email is optional but if present must be a string containing @. Print valid if there are no problems, otherwise print each problem field name on its own line in alphabetical order.", "import json\ndata = json.loads(input())\n# collect the invalid fields\n", `import json\ndata = json.loads(input())\nbad = []\nname = data.get("name")\nif not isinstance(name, str) or not name:\n    bad.append("name")\nage = data.get("age")\nif isinstance(age, bool) or not isinstance(age, int) or not 0 <= age <= 120:\n    bad.append("age")\nif "email" in data and (not isinstance(data["email"], str) or "@" not in data["email"]):\n    bad.append("email")\nprint("\\n".join(sorted(bad)) if bad else "valid")`, [["{\"name\": \"Asha\", \"age\": 20}", "valid"], ["{\"name\": \"\", \"age\": 200}", "age\nname"]], [["{\"name\": \"Asha\", \"age\": 20}", "valid"], ["{\"name\": \"\", \"age\": 200}", "age\nname"], ["{\"name\": \"A\", \"age\": 5, \"email\": \"a.in\"}", "email"], ["{\"age\": true}", "age\nname"], ["{\"name\": \"B\", \"age\": 0, \"email\": \"b@x.in\"}", "valid"], ["{\"name\": 5, \"age\": \"20\"}", "age\nname"]])],
});

