lessons.push({
  title: "API Testing, Swagger and OpenAPI Documentation",
  minutes: 50,
  learn: ["Write automated tests for API endpoints", "Use curl and test clients to explore an API", "Read and produce an OpenAPI description", "Test success, validation errors, authentication and edge cases"],
  why: "An API without tests breaks silently when changed, and one without documentation cannot be used by anyone else. OpenAPI gives you both a contract and a way to generate docs, clients and tests.",
  realWorld: "A CI pipeline runs 300 API tests on every commit; a mobile team generates a client library from the OpenAPI file.",
  simple: "Test the API from the outside like a client would: send requests, check status codes and bodies, including the bad cases. Describe the API in an <strong>OpenAPI</strong> document (paths, parameters, schemas) so tools such as <strong>Swagger UI</strong> can show and call it.",
  detail: `<h3>What to test</h3>
${table(["Case", "Example"], [["happy path", "create then read returns the same data (201 then 200)"], ["validation", "missing or invalid fields return 422 with the field names"], ["not found", "unknown id returns 404"], ["authentication", "no token 401; wrong role 403"], ["edge cases", "empty lists, very long text, duplicates (409), pagination limits"], ["idempotency", "PUT and DELETE twice"], ["contract", "response fields and types match the schema"]])}
<h3>pytest with a test client</h3>
<pre style="background:#16181c;color:#d8dee9;padding:12px 14px;border-radius:8px"><code>def test_create_student(client):\n    r = client.post("/students", json={"name": "Asha", "age": 20})\n    assert r.status_code == 201\n    assert r.json()["name"] == "Asha"</code></pre>
<p>Use a fresh in-memory database or reset state per test; make tests independent and fast; name them after behaviour. (Module 18 teaches pytest fully.)</p>
<h3>Manual exploration</h3>
${terminal("curl (needs a running server; shown, not executed here)", `$ curl -s http://localhost:8000/students/1\n$ curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8000/students \\\n    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\\n    -d '{"name": "Asha", "age": 20}'\n$ curl -i -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" http://localhost:8000/private`)}
<p>Postman, Insomnia, the Swagger UI <em>Try it out</em> button and VS Code's REST Client do the same with a graphical interface.</p>
<h3>OpenAPI</h3>
<p>An OpenAPI document (JSON or YAML) lists <code>paths</code>, each with methods, <code>parameters</code>, <code>requestBody</code> and <code>responses</code> (status code to schema), plus reusable <code>components.schemas</code>. FastAPI generates it from your code (<code>/openapi.json</code>); with Flask use extensions such as <code>flask-smorest</code> or <code>apispec</code>. <strong>Swagger UI</strong> and <strong>ReDoc</strong> render it; code generators create clients and server stubs; tools like Schemathesis fuzz the API from the schema.</p>
<p>Write meaningful summaries, descriptions and examples in the docs: the schema is the contract between teams.</p>`,
  syntax: { code: `# openapi.json (shape)\n{"openapi": "3.1.0", "info": {"title": "...", "version": "1.0"},\n "paths": {"/students": {"get": {...}, "post": {...}}},\n "components": {"schemas": {...}}}`, lang: "json" },
  diagram: chain("API development loop", "Left to right: design the contract in OpenAPI, implement the endpoint, test with a client, publish the docs and clients.",
    [{ k: "proc", t: "design\ncontract" }, { k: "proc", t: "implement\nendpoint" }, { k: "proc", t: "test\n(pytest, client)" }, { k: "term", t: "publish docs\n/docs" }], { w: 135, gap: 30, hgt: 58 }),
  example: { code: `from fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, Depends, Header\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\napp = FastAPI(title="Tasks API", version="0.1")\ntasks = {}\n\nclass TaskIn(BaseModel):\n    title: str = Field(min_length=1, description="What needs doing")\n    done: bool = False\n\ndef current_user(authorization: str = Header(default="")):\n    if authorization != "Bearer good-token":\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail="not authenticated")\n    return "asha"\n\n@app.post("/tasks", status_code=201, summary="Create a task")\ndef create(task: TaskIn, user: str = Depends(current_user)):\n    task_id = len(tasks) + 1\n    tasks[task_id] = {"id": task_id, **task.model_dump(), "owner": user}\n    return tasks[task_id]\n\n@app.get("/tasks/{task_id}")\ndef read(task_id: int, user: str = Depends(current_user)):\n    if task_id not in tasks:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail="task not found")\n    return tasks[task_id]\n\nclient = TestClient(app)\nAUTH = {"Authorization": "Bearer good-token"}\n\ndef run(name, check):\n    print(("PASS " if check() else "FAIL ") + name)\n\nrun("rejects missing token", lambda: client.post("/tasks", json={"title": "x"}).status_code == 401)\ncreated = client.post("/tasks", json={"title": "write tests"}, headers=AUTH)\nrun("creates a task", lambda: created.status_code == 201 and created.json()["done"] is False)\nrun("reads it back", lambda: client.get("/tasks/1", headers=AUTH).json()["title"] == "write tests")\nrun("404 for unknown", lambda: client.get("/tasks/99", headers=AUTH).status_code == 404)\nrun("422 for empty title", lambda: client.post("/tasks", json={"title": ""}, headers=AUTH).status_code == 422)\n\nschema = client.get("/openapi.json").json()\nprint(schema["info"], sorted(schema["paths"]))\npost = schema["paths"]["/tasks"]["post"]\nprint(post["summary"], sorted(post["responses"]))\nprint(sorted(schema["components"]["schemas"]["TaskIn"]["properties"]))`, out: `PASS rejects missing token\nPASS creates a task\nPASS reads it back\nPASS 404 for unknown\nPASS 422 for empty title\n{'title': 'Tasks API', 'version': '0.1'} ['/tasks', '/tasks/{task_id}']\nCreate a task ['201', '422']\n['done', 'title']` },
  lineByLine: [["current_user dependency", "Authentication shared by all endpoints; missing token gives 401."], ["run(name, check)", "A miniature test runner: pytest does this with assert and much better reports."], ["created.json()[\"done\"] is False", "Checks the default value in the contract."], ["schema[\"paths\"]", "The generated OpenAPI document lists the endpoints."], ["post[\"responses\"]", "Documented outcomes: 201 and 422 (validation)."], ["components.schemas.TaskIn", "The request body schema built from the Pydantic model."]],
  dryRun: { intro: "The test pyramid for an API:", headers: ["Level", "Speed", "Scope"], rows: [["unit tests of business logic", "fastest", "functions without HTTP"], ["API tests with a test client", "fast", "routes, validation, auth, database"], ["end-to-end tests", "slowest", "real server, network, browser"]] },
  realExample: { intro: "Reading an OpenAPI document to list operations, like a tool that generates docs or a client.", code: `import json\nspec = json.loads('{"openapi": "3.1.0", "info": {"title": "Demo", "version": "1"}, "paths": {"/students": {"get": {"summary": "List students"}, "post": {"summary": "Create a student"}}, "/students/{id}": {"get": {"summary": "Get one"}, "delete": {"summary": "Remove"}}}}')\nfor path in sorted(spec["paths"]):\n    for method in sorted(spec["paths"][path]):\n        print(method.upper().ljust(7), path, "-", spec["paths"][path][method]["summary"])`, out: `GET     /students - List students\nPOST    /students - Create a student\nDELETE  /students/{id} - Remove\nGET     /students/{id} - Get one` },
  mistakes: ["Testing only the happy path.", "Tests that depend on each other or on leftover data.", "Docs that drift from the code (generate them).", "No authentication tests.", "Asserting on whole bodies including volatile values such as timestamps."],
  practices: ["Test status code and the important body fields.", "Generate documentation from the code.", "Run API tests in CI on every change."],
  interview: ["How do you test an API?", "What is OpenAPI/Swagger?", "What would you test for an authenticated endpoint?", "Unit vs integration vs end-to-end tests?"],
  practiceQs: ["Write four test cases for DELETE /students/{id}.", "What does the responses section of OpenAPI describe?", "Why generate docs instead of writing them by hand?", "What does curl -i show?"],
  revision: ["Test happy path, validation, 404, auth, edges.", "Test client or pytest; fresh state per test.", "OpenAPI: paths, parameters, requestBody, responses, components.", "Swagger UI/ReDoc render it; generate clients."],
  hinglish: "API ko bahar se test karo: sahi data, galat data (422), na mila (404), bina token (401) aur edge cases. OpenAPI ek document hai jisme saare endpoints, parameters aur responses likhe hote hain, aur Swagger UI usse dikhata hai. FastAPI ye khud bana deta hai.",
  quiz: [
    mcq("Which status should a missing token produce?", ["200", "401", "404", "422"], 1, "Not authenticated."),
    mcq("What does an OpenAPI document describe?", ["An API's paths, parameters and responses", "A database schema only", "Server hardware", "A Python package"], 0, "It is the API contract."),
    mcq("What does Swagger UI provide?", ["An interactive page to read and try the API", "A database", "A load balancer", "A compiler"], 0, "Rendered from OpenAPI."),
    mcq("Why should each test start from clean state?", ["So tests are independent and repeatable", "It is faster to write", "pytest requires it", "To use less memory"], 0, "Order must not matter."),
    mcq("Where does FastAPI serve the schema?", ["/openapi.json", "/schema.txt", "/api.xml", "/swagger.py"], 0, "The OpenAPI JSON.")
  ],
  tasks: [task("Summarise an OpenAPI document", "Read one line holding an OpenAPI JSON document. Print one line per operation in the form METHOD PATH (method in capitals), ordered by path and then by method. Only get, post, put, patch and delete count as operations.", "import json\nspec = json.loads(input())\n# list the operations\n", `import json\nspec = json.loads(input())\nOPS = {"get", "post", "put", "patch", "delete"}\nfor path in sorted(spec["paths"]):\n    for method in sorted(spec["paths"][path]):\n        if method in OPS:\n            print(method.upper(), path)`, [["{\"openapi\": \"3.1.0\", \"paths\": {\"/students\": {\"get\": {}, \"post\": {}}, \"/students/{id}\": {\"delete\": {}, \"get\": {}}}}", "GET /students\nPOST /students\nDELETE /students/{id}\nGET /students/{id}"], ["{\"paths\": {\"/a\": {\"parameters\": [], \"put\": {}}}}", "PUT /a"]], [["{\"openapi\": \"3.1.0\", \"paths\": {\"/students\": {\"get\": {}, \"post\": {}}, \"/students/{id}\": {\"delete\": {}, \"get\": {}}}}", "GET /students\nPOST /students\nDELETE /students/{id}\nGET /students/{id}"], ["{\"paths\": {\"/a\": {\"parameters\": [], \"put\": {}}}}", "PUT /a"], ["{\"paths\": {\"/z\": {\"get\": {}}, \"/b\": {\"patch\": {}, \"get\": {}}}}", "GET /b\nPATCH /b\nGET /z"], ["{\"paths\": {\"/x\": {\"summary\": \"s\", \"delete\": {}}}}", "DELETE /x"]])],
});

module.exports = {
  module: {
    title: "Phase 4 - APIs and Web Development",
    description: "HTTP fundamentals, REST and JSON design, the requests library, integration patterns (retries, pagination, caching), Flask and FastAPI, authentication with password hashing and JWT, and API testing with OpenAPI and Swagger.",
    chapters: [{ title: "APIs and Web Development", description: "Building and consuming web APIs safely.", lessons }],
    assessment: {
      title: "Module 17 Assessment: APIs and Web Development",
      description: "Standard-library problems on HTTP, URLs, pagination and authentication headers.",
      questions: [
        task("Classify status codes", "Read a line of HTTP status codes. Print each on its own line as code class, where class is success (2xx), redirect (3xx), client error (4xx), server error (5xx) or other.", "", `for code in map(int, input().split()):\n    if 200 <= code < 300:\n        kind = "success"\n    elif 300 <= code < 400:\n        kind = "redirect"\n    elif 400 <= code < 500:\n        kind = "client error"\n    elif 500 <= code < 600:\n        kind = "server error"\n    else:\n        kind = "other"\n    print(code, kind)`, [["200 404 503", "200 success\n404 client error\n503 server error"], ["301 100", "301 redirect\n100 other"]], [["200 404 503", "200 success\n404 client error\n503 server error"], ["301 100", "301 redirect\n100 other"], ["201 204 299", "201 success\n204 success\n299 success"], ["399 400 499 500 599 600", "399 redirect\n400 client error\n499 client error\n500 server error\n599 server error\n600 other"]]),
        task("Build a query string", "Read n and then n lines key value. Print the URL query string with the pairs sorted by key (then by value) and percent-encoded using urllib.parse.urlencode with the default quoting (spaces become +).", "", `from urllib.parse import urlencode\nn = int(input())\npairs = [tuple(input().split(" ", 1)) for _ in range(n)]\nprint(urlencode(sorted(pairs)))`, [["2\nq python tips\npage 2", "page=2&q=python+tips"], ["1\ncity New Delhi", "city=New+Delhi"]], [["2\nq python tips\npage 2", "page=2&q=python+tips"], ["1\ncity New Delhi", "city=New+Delhi"], ["3\nb 2\na 1\na 0", "a=0&a=1&b=2"], ["1\nx a&b=c", "x=a%26b%3Dc"]]),
        task("Collect paginated results", "Read n, then n lines each holding one page as a JSON list. Pages arrive in order; stop at the first empty page (or the end of the input). Print the total number of items collected and then all items in order, separated by spaces.", "", `import json\nn = int(input())\nitems = []\nfor _ in range(n):\n    page = json.loads(input())\n    if not page:\n        break\n    items.extend(page)\nprint(len(items))\nprint(" ".join(map(str, items)))`, [["3\n[1, 2, 3]\n[4, 5]\n[]", "5\n1 2 3 4 5"], ["2\n[7]\n[8, 9]", "3\n7 8 9"]], [["3\n[1, 2, 3]\n[4, 5]\n[]", "5\n1 2 3 4 5"], ["2\n[7]\n[8, 9]", "3\n7 8 9"], ["3\n[1]\n[]\n[2]", "1\n1"], ["1\n[10, 20]", "2\n10 20"]]),
        task("Basic auth header", "Read a username and a password (two lines). Print the HTTP header line Authorization: Basic <token>, where token is the base64 of username:password.", "", `import base64\nuser = input()\npassword = input()\ntoken = base64.b64encode(f"{user}:{password}".encode()).decode()\nprint("Authorization: Basic " + token)`, [["aladdin\nopen sesame", "Authorization: Basic YWxhZGRpbjpvcGVuIHNlc2FtZQ=="], ["asha\npw1", "Authorization: Basic YXNoYTpwdzE="]], [["aladdin\nopen sesame", "Authorization: Basic YWxhZGRpbjpvcGVuIHNlc2FtZQ=="], ["asha\npw1", "Authorization: Basic YXNoYTpwdzE="], ["a\nb", "Authorization: Basic YTpi"], ["user\np:w", "Authorization: Basic dXNlcjpwOnc="]]),
      ],
    },
  },
};
